From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: tolerate an unavailable power-service title

The native proxy can exist before UPower initializes the battery title.
Keep the existing visibility policy and render empty text until it is ready.
GPL-2.0-or-later, following GNOME Shell upstream.

diff --git a/js/ui/status/system.js b/js/ui/status/system.js
--- a/js/ui/status/system.js
+++ b/js/ui/status/system.js
@@ -461,7 +461,7 @@
             const seconds = proxy.State === UPower.DeviceState.CHARGING ? proxy.TimeToFull : proxy.TimeToEmpty;
             const hours = Math.floor(seconds / 3600), minutes = Math.floor(seconds % 3600 / 60);
             const remaining = seconds > 0 ? (hours ? _('%d h %d min').format(hours, minutes) : _('%d min').format(minutes)) : '';
-            const percentage = GLib.markup_escape_text(this._powerToggle.title, -1);
+            const percentage = GLib.markup_escape_text(this._powerToggle.title ?? '', -1);
             const suffix = remaining ? ` · ${remaining} ` +
                 (proxy.State === UPower.DeviceState.CHARGING ? _('until full') : _('left')) : '';
             label.clutter_text.set_markup(`<span weight="650" alpha="65535">${percentage}</span>${GLib.markup_escape_text(suffix, -1)}`);
